---
description: Three.js Guidelines
globs: *.js, *.jsx
---
- Use ES6 modules for importing Three.js and its components.
- Implement `requestAnimationFrame` for smooth rendering loops.
- Utilize Three.js's built-in controls like `OrbitControls` for camera manipulation.
- Optimize 3D models and textures for web performance.
- Use `Object3D.frustumCulled` for objects that may go out of view.
- Implement level of detail (LOD) for complex 3D models.
- Use `THREE.BufferGeometry` instead of `THREE.Geometry` for better performance.
- Implement object pooling for frequently created and destroyed objects.
- Use `THREE.Raycaster` for mouse picking in 3D scenes.
- Implement custom cursors using CSS for different interactions.
- Use event listeners for mouse movements and clicks.